Template: mountbridge/add-installing-user
Type: boolean
Default: true
_Description: Allow ${user} to mount NFS and SMB shares?
 MountBridge mounts NFS and SMB/CIFS shares through a small root helper that
 only members of the "mountbridge" group may run.
 .
 If you accept, ${user} is added to that group; it takes effect at their next
 login. Other users can be given access later with "adduser <user>
 mountbridge", or from within MountBridge. SSHFS mounts need no special access.

Template: mountbridge/installing-user
Type: string
Description: for internal use
 The user who ran the installation, passed from the config script to postinst.
